GUI(1)

NAME
    gui - start the graphical shell

SYNOPSIS
    gui

DESCRIPTION
    Starts the SmallOS graphical user interface.

    The desktop includes Files, Shell, System, Config, About, and Quit icons.
    Shell windows run child shells through PTYs. Window dragging is frame-paced
    while cursor movement stays immediate.

    The Config window stores GUI settings in /etc/gui.conf when the mounted
    filesystem is writable. The current USB mass-storage boot path is read-only,
    so those settings are not preserved across reboots there yet.

    The Config window can toggle the GUI perf readout. The readout is off by
    default.
